

{ Models

  { Sentence Transformers

   *Sentence transformers* (a.k.a. bi-encoder) models calculate a *fixed-size* vector representation (embedding) given texts, images, audio, or video.
    
    Using embeddings is typically efficient. Especially, similarity calculations are fast.

    Embedings can be used for tasks such as
      • semantic textual similarity,
      • semantic search,
      • clustering,
      • classification,
      • paraphrase mining,
      • and more.

    Calculating the embedding is often the *first step* in a retrieval environment (where a *cross-encoder*, a.k.a. reranker model is used to
    find the top-k results from the be-encoder).

    See also the Python library `sentence-transformer`.

